    "title": "A Limited Dragon Ball Pop-Up Tour Is Coming to Illinois First - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Quaid ,\n8 hours ago\nDragon Ball is a multi-generational story spanning back to its beginning in the 1980s and catching fire in the United States in the 1990s. Celebrate the 40 th anniversary of the adventures of Goku , Krillin and Master Roshi and all their friends and foes at a limited Dragon Ball pop-up tour that is only making weekend stops in five places, and it all begins in Illinois at the Woodfield Mall Friday, February 6 th .\nWoodfield Mall – Schaumburg, Illinois will be the first stop on the limited tour Woodfield Mall – Schaumburg, Illinois/Google Street View Read More: Pokemon’s 30th Anniversary Festival is Coming to St. Louis\nWhether your Dragon Ball fandom comes from the manga, anime, or video games, there is so much lore and history to the franchise, along with worldwide fans of all ages that an opportunity to celebrate all things Dragon Ball with fellow fans is an experience to be grasped.\nSubscribe to KICK FM, #1 For New Country on Youtube\nThings to look for at the Schaumburg, Illinois weekend stop include loads of merchandise, including hard to find items. Video game displays and the Dragon Ball Super card game, with tutorials and giveaways, plus limited-edition personal build Goku models.\nDownload the KICK Mobile App Now Dragon Ball has been around long enough that parents have introduced their kids to the stories, characters and games. An opportunity to celebrate a passion that parents and kids both have is rare. 40 years in the making, and only in a few locations. Don’t miss the chance to be in the middle of it all.\nMORE: See 30 toys that every '90s kid wanted Image of\nThings You'd Find in Every 90s Home Back in the Day The tell-tale signs of a home in the '90s. Gallery Credit: Danielle Kootman Canva Wood Paneling Ah, yes, the wood paneling. No '90s home would be complete without it. Canva Beige Everything Couches, lamps, paint everything had a nice yellow, tan glow to it. Canva Brass Fixtures Door knobs, lights, sinks, all brass. Canva Oak Cabinets Before white and colored cabinets were a thing, it was all about that oak. augustv123, YouTube Water Beds Get in and sink in. These were great if you wanted to feel like you were sleeping on a raft. See more stylish designs here. Canva Large Sound Systems/Speakers The bigger, the better. Canva Phones with Cords Remember the phone on your kitchen wall with the super long cord? No private phone calls in those days. Canva Ivy If it wasn't a plant above your cabinets, it was a design on your wall. Canva/ Beverley Hills 90210, YouTube Bulky Electronics From VHS and heavy televisions to the giant entertainment centers they were on, sleek wasn't the thing back then. But, at least you could watch Beverly Hills 90210 . Canva Thick Carpets Homes had to have that thick carpet (beige in color, of course.) Canva Floral Prints If it wasn't on your walls, it was on your couch.\n1",
    "summary": "Dragon Ball is a multi-generational story spanning back to its beginning in the 1980s and catching fire in the United States in the 1990s. Celebrate the 40 th anniversary of the adventures of Goku , Krillin and Master Roshi and all their friends and foes at a limited Dragon Ball pop-up tour that is only making weekend stops in five places, and it all begins in Illinois at the Woodfield Mall Friday, February 6 th .",
